### Reason for failure (if possible)

**1. LoadBalancer test: AWS Classic ELB registered-instance cap**

The AWS cloud-controller-manager log shows the same error on every 5 min retry (latest run, pod `aws-cloud-controller-manager-6c4rg`):

```
W aws.go:2801] Error registering instances with the load balancer: "operation error Elastic Load Balancing: RegisterInstancesWithLoadBalancer, https response error StatusCode: 400, ... api error ValidationError: The maximum number of instances on load balancer 'ae75ae0b4f4ca413d8839f9058c4b9ab' has been reached"
```

The CCM creates a Classic ELB and registers all 2000 workers on it. The AWS default quota is 1,000 registered instances per Classic Load Balancer, adjustable through Service Quotas (https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/classic/elb-limits.html). The Service never gets an ingress, the test waits the full large-cluster timeout (`loadBalancerCreateTimeoutLarge`, 60 min) and fails at https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/8820bafbb164954dfc874e6a5102a9b1d298e2ce/test/e2e/apps/deployment.go#L1413. The same error is in the 2026-10-07 run, so this has been true from day one.

**2. Topology Hints test: stale cross-zone hints once the Service spans more than one EndpointSlice**

The cluster meets the test's preconditions: three zones, all nodes Ready, equal allocatable CPU. The test creates a DaemonSet on every node plus a Service with `service.kubernetes.io/topology-mode: Auto`, waits until the EndpointSlices hold 2000 endpoints, then asserts once, with no retry, that every endpoint has exactly one hint and that it equals the endpoint's own zone (https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/8820bafbb164954dfc874e6a5102a9b1d298e2ce/test/e2e/network/topology_hints.go#L143-L159). The failure is always the same-zone check, with a different zone each run:

```
[FAILED] Expected endpoint in topology-hints-28sc9 to have same zone hint, got us-east-2a: {... ForZones:[]ForZone{ForZone{Name:us-east-2b,},},...}
```

KCM log: hints were enabled one second after the Service appeared (`Insufficient number of endpoints (0 endpoints, 3 zones), removing hints` at 00:52:15, `Topology Aware Hints has been enabled, adding hints.` at 00:52:16) while the 2000 DaemonSet pods were still arriving over about 20 s (284, 793, 1269, 1767, 2000 nodes available).

Mechanism in `staging/src/k8s.io/endpointslice/topologycache` at the build SHA:

- `AddHints` recomputes hints only for the slices in `ToCreate` and `ToUpdate`. Slices in `Unchanged` keep their existing hints as long as every ready endpoint has a hint for a zone with allocations and the per-zone totals stay at or below `allocation.maximum` (`getAllocatedHintsByZone` / `getHintsByZone`).
- With `overloadThreshold = 0.2`, the band for 2000 endpoints over three equal zones is minimum 556 and maximum 889 hints per zone. Many cross-zone assignments fit inside that band.
- `EndpointsEqualBeyondHash` (https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/8820bafbb164954dfc874e6a5102a9b1d298e2ce/staging/src/k8s.io/endpointslice/util/controller_utils.go#L299) ignores `Hints`, so a slice whose endpoints did not change is never rewritten. Cross-zone hints assigned during the skewed early batches persist for the life of the slice.
- `redistributeHints` only moves hints between slices that are already being written.

At 100 nodes the Service fits in one slice (`maxEndpointsPerSlice` 100), and that slice is rewritten on every reconcile, so the end state is always same-zone. At 2000 nodes there are 20 slices.

A simulation that drives the real `TopologyCache.AddHints` with the reconciler's packing rules (`reconcileByPortMapping`, `getSliceToFill`) at the build SHA gives (5 seeds each, source at the end):

| Scenario | Slices | Endpoints with a cross-zone hint |
|---|---|---|
| 100 nodes, incremental arrival | 1 | 0 |
| 300 nodes, incremental arrival | 3 | 6 to 22 |
| 1000 nodes, incremental arrival | 10 | 24 to 56 |
| 2000 nodes, batches of 50 | 20 | 94 to 113 |
| 2000 nodes, batches of exactly 100 | 20 | 101 to 109 |
| 2000 nodes, all in one reconcile (control) | 20 | 0 |

A final no-op reconcile rewrote zero slices in every case, so the state is permanent. Per-zone hint totals end at exactly 667/666/667, which is what the controller promises. The test asserts a stronger property that only holds while the whole Service fits in one slice. The same failure is expected on any multi-zone cluster with more than about 100 schedulable nodes.

**3. API connection resets**

The apiserver did not restart after bootstrap, the control-plane node shows no OOM, and the apiserver log roll at 01:01 is a rotation. No leader-election loss in KCM or CCM. In k8s-triage this signature appears only in the ec2 scale-correctness 100 and 2000 jobs. The 100 node tab (`ec2-master-scale-correctness-100`) is FLAKY mostly because of it. The cause is not determined. NLB target reset counts and health-check flaps around the failure timestamps would be the next thing to look at.

